<Base
  title="Northstack · Informal Engineer"
  description="Managed hosting for the self-hosted apps you want without the maintenance. Join the waitlist and tell us which app you'd want hosted."
>
  <h1>Northstack</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Every guide on this site ends with you running your own infrastructure.
    Northstack is for the day you want the app without the maintenance:
    managed hosting for the same open-source tools, run on the same
    density-tested setups the Lab Notes document in public.
  </p>

  <p class="section-label">how it works</p>
  <p class="lede">
    It's being built in the open right now, tenant density economics and all
    (watch the <a href="/notes/">Lab Notes</a> and <a href="/research/">research
    lines</a>). The waitlist shapes the roadmap directly: the apps people ask
    for first get built first.
  </p>

  <p class="section-label">join the waitlist</p>
  <p class="lede">
    One email, two questions worth of effort:
  </p>
  <a
    href="mailto:MeshaelR@gmail.com?subject=Northstack%20waitlist&body=Which%20app%20would%20you%20want%20hosted%3F%0A%0AWhat%20do%20you%20run%20today%20(if%20anything)%3F"
    style="display: inline-block; background: var(--accent); color: #101214; padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 5px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500;"
  >
    Join by email
  </a>
  <p style="font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--faint); margin-top: 0.75rem;">
    (A proper form is coming with the newsletter platform. The mailto works
    today and a human reads it, which is more than most waitlists offer.)
  </p>
</Base>
